@startuml
' LSP connection finite-state machine: 7 states, 17 transitions.
' This is the single source of truth in lib.lsp.fsm and the anchor of the
' source<->formal alignment gate (see docs/formal/verification-gate.md).
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #3B7A3B
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #D4EDD0
  BorderColor #3B7A3B
  FontColor #123312
}

[*] --> disconnected

disconnected --> connecting : StartConnect

connecting --> connected : OpenSocket (onopen)
connecting --> error : SocketError
connecting --> disconnected : UnexpectedClose

connected --> initializing : send `initialize`
connected --> disconnecting : StartShutdown
connected --> error : SocketError

initializing --> initialized : InitializeResponse
initializing --> disconnecting : StartShutdown
initializing --> error : SocketError
initializing --> disconnected : UnexpectedClose

initialized --> disconnecting : StartShutdown
initialized --> error : SocketError
initialized --> disconnected : UnexpectedClose

disconnecting --> disconnected : ShutdownClosed (exit + close)

error --> disconnected : cleanup
error --> connecting : Reconnect (backoff)

note right of initialized
  Derived flags (connected? / initialized? /
  connecting? / reachable?) are PROJECTIONS of
  this state — never written directly.
  connected? holds for: connected, initializing,
  initialized.
end note

note bottom of disconnecting
  Graceful shutdown sets :shutting-down? so
  UnexpectedClose does NOT trigger auto-reconnect.
end note
@enduml
